('advanced-native-1210', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1210-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It was useful support, but relying on it alone made unusual requests easier to miss."],"options":["The speaker abandoned the checklist and now works from memory alone.","The speaker now uses the checklist to avoid asking about unusual cases.","The difficulty was caused by checking too many unusual requests with other people.","It was useful support, but relying on it alone made unusual requests easier to miss."]},"advanced-native-1210-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It helped with routine reminders, but I needed to ask about exceptions.","I wanted to keep its useful prompts without replacing my attention to new information.","I was treating the list as if it covered unusual requests too.","I leaned on it too heavily instead of noticing what was missing."],"options":["It helped with routine reminders, but I needed to ask about exceptions.","I wanted to keep its useful prompts without replacing my attention to new information.","I was treating the list as if it covered unusual requests too.","I leaned on it too heavily instead of noticing what was missing."]},"advanced-native-1210-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["She can lean on her colleague for guidance while learning the process herself."],"options":["She can lean on her colleague for guidance while learning the process herself.","She is relying on her colleague to make the notes and handle the unclear cases for her.","The colleague’s explanation means she no longer needs to notice unfamiliar cases."]},"advanced-native-1210-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Every instance of leaning on support must be excessive."],"options":["A person may use reliable help while retaining responsibility.","Every instance of leaning on support must be excessive.","Too heavily adds a warning about the amount or role of reliance."]},"advanced-native-1210-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["I should not lean on it too heavi