('advanced-native-1212', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1212-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Both needs matter, but arranging them together creates a practical tension."],"options":["The two needs are described as identical, so no scheduling choice is needed.","Both needs matter, but arranging them together creates a practical tension.","The need to ask for help has been disproved by the need for quiet.","The speaker wants pupils to stop asking anyone for help."]},"advanced-native-1212-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Pupils need opportunities to ask for help as well as time to concentrate.","The plan has to respect two real needs that can compete for the same time.","Two truths rub against each other: pupils need quiet concentration, but they also need to ask for help.","Complete silence alone would leave the need for discussion unaddressed."],"options":["Pupils need opportunities to ask for help as well as time to concentrate.","The plan has to respect two real needs that can compete for the same time.","Two truths rub against each other: pupils need quiet concentration, but they also need to ask for help.","Complete silence alone would leave the need for discussion unaddressed."]},"advanced-native-1212-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Two truths rub against each other: the theatre needs income, and access matters too."],"options":["The need for income means the residents’ access is not a real concern.","Two truths rub against each other: the theatre needs income, and access matters too.","Concern about access shows that the theatre has no running costs."]},"advanced-native-1212-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["One statement must be false merely because the needs are difficult to combine."],"options":["One statement must be false merely because the needs are difficult to combine.","The speaker should explain the tension rather than just repeat the metaphor.","Both observations can be valid while creating a difficult choice."]},"advanced-native